msgid "Not recommended"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:787
msgid "Using this option prevents subscribers from having to repeatedly sign up for notifications when a product becomes available in limited quantities after going out of stock. For instance, if there are 100 subscribers signed up for notifications and only 10 units are expected to be restocked at a time, enabling this option ensures that those subscribers won't need to re-register for notifications each time the product is restocked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:789
msgid "Note: Enabling this option repeatedly sends instock notifications whenever a product becomes available until the subscribed product is \"purchased\" or \"unsubscribed.\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:800
msgid "When a product is restocked with only a few units, notify just the earliest subscribers instead of everyone. For example: 100 subscribers are waiting and you restock 5 units, only the first 5 subscribers are notified. The remaining 95 stay on the waitlist and are notified automatically on the next restock, they do not need to subscribe again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:802
msgid "Subscribers who already received a notification are moved to the end of the line, so everyone gets a fair turn. Applies only to automatic instock emails for products that manage stock quantity. Manual and bulk sends are never limited."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:815
msgid "How many subscribers to notify for each unit in stock. Default is 1, so restocking 5 units notifies the first 5 subscribers. Increase this if you expect that not every notified subscriber will buy. For example: set 2 and restocking 5 units notifies the first 10 subscribers. Used only when Fair Sending above is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:822
msgid "Please select background process engine, this is important to send a mail in background by default it is WP Background Process and you can also choose WooCommerce Background Process"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:830
msgid "Send automatic instock emails gradually instead of all at once. Useful when your hosting provider or SMTP service limits how many emails you can send per minute or hour. Emails over the limit are automatically sent in the following minutes, nothing is lost or skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:832
msgid "Applies only to automatic background emails. Manual sends, bulk sends and subscription confirmation emails are never delayed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:845
msgid "Maximum number of automatic instock emails to send per minute. Default is 60. Check your hosting or SMTP provider limits and set a slightly lower value. For example: a provider limit of 600 emails per hour means at most 10 per minute. Used only when Limit Email Sending Speed above is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:858
msgid "Subscribers are queued the moment a product is restocked, then emailed by a background task. If that task fails or never runs (for example when the server cron is not firing), those subscribers can get stuck without an email. When enabled, a recovery task periodically finds these stuck entries and tries to send their email again. Leave this off unless you actually see stuck entries, no background task is scheduled while it is off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:868
msgid "Every Hour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:869
msgid "Every 6 Hours"
msgstr ""

